class.description:
[CSV] converts comma-separated values ([url=https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4180]RFC 4180[/url]) to an [Array] of rows and back, with row, cell and column methods. Files with the extension [code].csv[/code] or [code].tsv[/code] load as [CSV]; for [code].tsv[/code] without [member TextDataFormat.options], the separator is a tab. Parsing, errors, [method TextDataFormat.load] and [method TextDataFormat.save] come from [TextDataFormat]; [method parse_string] and [method stringify] work on data without an instance, [method serialize] and [method deserialize] on resources.
Cells that contain the delimiter, a double quote, a line break or leading or trailing spaces are written in double quotes, and a double quote inside is doubled ([code]""[/code]). The delimiter comes from [member SerializerOptions.csv_delimiter] (one character, for example [code];[/code] or a tab).
The [member TextDataFormat.data] of an instance is an [Array] of rows, each row a [PackedStringArray]. With [member SerializerOptions.csv_headers] (the default), the first line names the columns: it is stored in [member header] and is not part of the data, and [method get_row_as_dictionary] keys a row by column name. Without it, [member header] is empty and every line is a data row. Columns are [int] indices; [method find_column] resolves a name. Cells are always [String]s, there is no type guessing ([code]007[/code] stays [code]"007"[/code]).
The static [method parse_string] returns an [Array] of [Dictionary] keyed by column name when headers are on, and an [Array] of [PackedStringArray] otherwise.
In the editor, a CSV file opens in the text editor and in the [b]Dataset[/b] bottom dock at the same time: cells are typed and checked by a [DataSchema] (found by [member DataSchema.file_patterns]), and both editors always show the same data. A translation CSV (imported as translation, or every header column after the first a locale, a [code]_[/code] note or [code]?context[/code]/[code]?plural[/code]) opens in the [b]Localization Table[/b] dock instead, where it is checked with [method validate_translation].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var csv = CSV.new()
if csv.parse("name,level\nAnn,3\n\"Bob, the 2nd\",7\n") == OK:
	for i in csv.get_row_count():
		print(csv.get_cell(i, csv.find_column("name")), " ", int(csv.get_cell(i, 1)))
else:
	print(csv.get_error_message()) # For example "Line 2: ..."; the line alone is csv.get_error_line().

print(CSV.stringify([{ "name": "Ann", "level": 3 }]))
# name,level
# Ann,3
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var csv = new Csv();
if (csv.Parse("name,level\nAnn,3\n\"Bob, the 2nd\",7\n") == Error.Ok)
{
	for (int i = 0; i < csv.GetRowCount(); i++)
	{
		GD.Print(csv.GetCell(i, csv.FindColumn("name")), " ", csv.GetCell(i, 1).ToInt());
	}
}
else
{
	GD.Print(csv.GetErrorMessage()); // For example "Line 2: ..."; the line alone is csv.GetErrorLine().
}

var rows = new Godot.Collections.Array { new Godot.Collections.Dictionary { { "name", "Ann" }, { "level", 3 } } };
GD.Print(Csv.Stringify(rows));
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Resource and files:[/b] [CSV] is a [Resource] (see [TextDataFormat]). [code]load("res://x.csv")[/code] of a plain file returns an instance, while files with a [code]$type[/code] marker load as the serialized resource. Plain files load with the project default options. The instance methods [method TextDataFormat.load] and [method TextDataFormat.save] work like [method ConfigFile.load] and [method ConfigFile.save]: they do not use the resource cache and do not set [member Resource.resource_path]. In exported games [code]res://[/code] is read-only, so save to [code]user://[/code].
[b]Changes:[/b] changing the data ([member TextDataFormat.data] in the inspector, [member TextDataFormat.data], [method set_cell], [method append_row] ...) drops the kept parsed text, so comments and formatting of the file are lost on the next save. [member TextDataFormat.options] set to [code]null[/code] uses the project settings.
[b]Import:[/b] In the editor, a [code].csv[/code] file whose header has locale columns is imported as a translation (importer "CSV Translation") and loads as [Translation]. Other CSV files use the "CSV Dataset" importer and load as [CSV]; so do files imported with [b]Keep File[/b].
[b]Note:[/b] The static methods can be called from any thread. A [CSV] instance should be used by one thread at a time.

method.description:
Validates the CSV as a translation table, with the rules of the CSV translation importer: column 0 holds the keys, columns named [code]?context[/code] and [code]?plural[/code] hold the message context and plural form, columns starting with [code]_[/code] are ignored, all other columns are locales. Rows whose key is [code]?pluralrule[/code] and rows without a key (further plural forms) are not checked. The importer uses the same header checks.
The result contains:
- [constant DataValidation.ISSUE_KIND_INVALID_LOCALE] for a header cell that is no locale (the importer ignores the column), for a locale whose language code is unknown (the importer imports it anyway), and once without a position when no column starts with a known language code (the file is no translation table; rows are not checked then).
- [constant DataValidation.ISSUE_KIND_DUPLICATE_KEY] for a second [code]?context[/code] or [code]?plural[/code] column, and for a key used twice in the same context (the later row replaces the earlier one on import).
- [constant DataValidation.ISSUE_KIND_EMPTY_REQUIRED] for each missing translation: an empty locale cell in a row with a key. The field of the issue is the name of the locale column.
- [constant DataValidation.ISSUE_KIND_MISSING_FIELD] if the CSV has no [member header].
Rows and columns are 0-based ([code]row[/code] counts data rows, without the header); header issues have no row. With [member DataValidationOptions.keep_positions] and text kept by [method TextDataFormat.parse], issues also get their line.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var csv = CSV.new()
csv.parse(FileAccess.get_file_as_string("res://translations/ui.csv"))
var result = csv.validate_translation()
for i in result.get_issue_count():
    print(result.get_issue_message(i))
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var csv = new Csv();
csv.Parse(FileAccess.GetFileAsString("res://translations/ui.csv"));
DataValidation result = csv.ValidateTranslation();
for (int i = 0; i < result.GetIssueCount(); i++)
{
    GD.Print(result.GetIssueMessage(i));
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
